{{- /*
  The account the onepassword* template functions are given, as JSON: "my" on Linux and Android,
  and none on Windows, where op takes it from OP_ACCOUNT (`env:` in .chezmoi.yaml.tmpl) instead.
  Every 1Password call passes it as its account argument, never "my" itself:
      {{- $op := includeTemplate "lib-onepassword.tmpl" . | fromJson -}}
      {{- $item := onepassword $name "Private" $op.account -}}

  An account argument makes chezmoi run `op account list` before its first 1Password call. On
  Windows the 1Password app removes the pipe op connects to for about 0.9 s after that call, so the
  `op signin` chezmoi runs straight after fails with "cannot connect to 1Password app, make sure it
  is running". Without an account chezmoi runs no `account list`, and the calls after an approved
  one meet no gap. WSL keeps the account: its op wrapper retries that failure. See "1Password CLI
  Retry" in AGENTS.md.

  onepasswordRead takes its account as an optional argument, and an empty one still goes through
  `account list`, which then matches no account. Give it the account only when there is one:
      {{ if $op.account }}{{ onepasswordRead $url $op.account }}{{ else }}{{ onepasswordRead $url }}{{ end }}
*/ -}}
{{- dict "account" (ternary "" "my" (eq .chezmoi.os "windows")) | toJson -}}
